---
title: File headers
tags: tools
summary: >-
    Lists common file headers in hex, the bytes that files of each type start with, to quickly match a chunk of data to a file type.
noLimits: true
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>To match a file's header for you, use <a href="/files/check/" class="text-convrtr">Check file type</a>.</p>
    <p><code class="tool-example">??</code> stands for any byte, so a header that starts partway into the file is written where it sits. Filter by name, extension or hex: the hex can be written with or without spaces.</p>
    <p>More on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_file_signatures" class="text-convrtr">File signatures</a> Wikipedia page.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
<div class="tool-frame">
    <div class="tool-frame__stack">
        <div class="file-headers__filter">
            <div class="input-group">
                <label class="input-group-text" for="{{ filename }}Filter"><i class="bi bi-search" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">Filter file headers</span></label>
                <input type="search" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Filter" placeholder="Name, extension or hex, such as png or 89 50" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Count">
            </div>
            <span class="tool-pane__status" id="{{ filename }}Count" role="status">{{ headers | length }} file types</span>
        </div>
        <div class="file-headers" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="{{ filename }}Caption">
            <table class="file-headers__table">
                <caption class="visually-hidden" id="{{ filename }}Caption">File headers: each file type, the bytes it starts with, and its usual extensions</caption>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">File type</th>
                        <th scope="col">Header</th>
                        <th scope="col">Extensions</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    {%- for header in headers %}
                    <tr data-search="{{ [header.name, header.description, header.extensions] | join(' ') | lower }}"
                        data-hex="{{ header.hex | join('|') | replace(' ', '') | replace('??', '|') | lower }}">
                        <th scope="row">{{ header.name }}<small>{{ header.description }}</small></th>
                        <td class="file-headers__hex">
                            {%- for item in header.hex %}
                            <span>{{ item | replace("??", '<span class="file-headers__any">??</span>') | safe }}</span>
                            {%- endfor %}
                        </td>
                        <td>{{ header.extensions or "—" }}</td>
                    </tr>
                    {%- endfor %}
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="file-headers__empty" id="{{ filename }}Empty" hidden>No file types match</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endcall %}
